<title>USA: Embrex says U.K. says no to vaccine for now.</title>
<headline>Embrex says U.K. says no to vaccine for now.</headline>
<dateline>RESEARCH TRIANGLE PARK, N.C. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Embrex Inc said Thursday a drug for chickens containing the company's viral neutralizing factor has been provisionally refused approval by British authorities.</p>
<p>The company said British authorities have asked for more information on Bursamune before rendering a final decision.</p>
<p>Bursamune, a vaccine for avian bursal disease, is produced by a unit of American Home Products Corp, Ft. Dodge Animal Health, and Ft. Dodge's Australian affiliate, Cyanamid Websters.</p>
<p>The company said it had anticipated approval by mid 1997.</p>
</text>
